# src/cs1090a_spec_driven_development/py.typed
# PEP 561 INLINE TYPE MARKER.
#
# WITHOUT THIS FILE THIS PACKAGE IS UNTYPED TO EVERY CONSUMER, including our own
# test suite. mypy resolves an import through src/ while the module exists
# there, but falls through to the INSTALLED distribution otherwise -- and an
# installed package with no marker is reported as "missing library stubs or
# py.typed marker" no matter how completely it is annotated.
#
# THE FAILURE IS THEREFORE INTERMITTENT BY CONSTRUCTION, which is why it went
# unnoticed until a test imported a module that had not been written yet: every
# other import happened to resolve from source. A consumer installing the wheel
# would have hit it on the first import.
#
# THE FILE'S CONTENT IS IGNORED; only its presence in the package directory
# matters, and hatchling includes it because it sits inside the package. This
# comment therefore costs nothing and explains why an apparently empty file is
# load-bearing.
